    // the expected value of p^X after k steps, where X is the exponent.
    // The transition: if current exponent is i, next exponent j (0 <= j <= i)
    // is chosen with probability 1/(i+1).
    // So E[p^X_{t+1} | X_t = i] = (1/(i+1)) * sum_{j=0}^{i} p^j
    // We want E[p^X_k] starting from X_0 = e.
    //
    // Let dp[t][i] = E[p^X_t | X_0 = i]
    // dp[0][i] = p^i
    // dp[t+1][i] = (1/(i+1)) * sum_{j=0}^{i} dp[t][j]
    //
